<!--
  The Kaaba, as a mark on the Qibla dial: the silhouette. Its band and door are a separate
  drawable, ic_kaaba_detail.xml, drawn on top of this one in the dial's own face colour.

  Shared between the phone and the watch, because they draw the same dial twice and a
  shape that drifts between them is exactly the kind of gap this project has been bitten
  by before.

  Two drawables rather than one path with the band and door cut out of it by the even-odd
  rule. The cut-out version was written first and looked correct in review, and it was
  wrong: a hole shows whatever is behind the mark, and what is behind the mark is the
  needle. The Qibla needle ends inside the cube, so it appeared as a green streak through
  the doorway and across the band, which read as a rendering fault rather than a building.
  Opaque silhouette plus opaque detail cannot do that, whatever it is drawn over.

  Deliberately a flat elevation and not a photograph or a perspective render. A photograph
  would be someone else's copyright, would weigh more than the rest of the app's drawables
  put together, and would be unreadable at the ~19dp this is drawn at on a 1.2" watch. The
  silhouette, the band and the raised door are the three things that make it recognisable;
  everything else is detail that disappears at that size anyway.

  Geometry, in the 24x24 viewport: the wall is x 4.5..19.5 and y 3..20, so 15 wide by 17
  tall — very slightly taller than it is wide, which is the proportion of the real face
  that carries the door. It stands on the wider marble plinth, the shadharwan, at y 20.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FF000000"
        android:pathData="M4.5,3h15v17h-15z M3,20h18v1.5h-18z" />
</vector>
